{"duration_api_ms":168174,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ed901c09-4ea5-46c4-94d4-d0eef1b23367","total_cost_usd":0.219268,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16096,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10930},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16096,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15488,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16096},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15488,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16096,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.219268,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10930,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially a one-dimensional flight-path-angle sweep at the corner design D≈3.385 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70°. Along it, flux rises from 227k to 274.5k W/m2 and bondline temperature falls from 417.9 K to 391.1 K as gamma goes from -1.5° to -3.57°. Diameter is capped by the mass-fraction limit: the margin is 1.4e-4 at D=3.385 and 2.7e-5 at D=3.3852, and it falls about 0.59 per metre, so the limit sits at D≈3.38524. Gamma is capped by max_g (about 12 g at gamma≈-3.570). Every bluntness or cone move away from (1.2, 70) either lowered the mass-fraction margin or produced a 'cd_fore' extrapolation failure. All 33 no-geometry failures I can see in the data are extrapolation failures at bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-7fdf9581b717 (D 3.3852, gamma -3.569) is feasible with max_g margin 2.0e-4 and mass margin 2.7e-5, so it sits at both binding limits.\",\"C-6146d28a8413, C-2a109f1c4205, C-053e6577c074 and C-3583b7488cf2 all have max_g margin below 0 at gamma -3.58 to -3.6, so the g cap is about -3.570.\",\"C-67c092ae8706 and C-b80fd27a21c5 (bluntness 1.1 and 1.15, cone 69.5 and 69.3) have negative mass margin at D≈3.38, so lowering bluntness or cone hurts.\",\"C-4aa35af3d6a3, C-39bfab3c832b, C-460ff98d4dde, C-02bec3a7a6f4 and C-35e288c12205 fail the cd_fore hull check at bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70, so the surrogate domain edge is at the corner.\",\"The front points at D 3.385 (C-948029610632 through C-7fdf9581b717) give a smooth monotone flux/temperature curve in gamma that I can interpolate.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Flux and bondline temperature trade off through gamma alone. A shallower entry lowers peak dynamic pressure and flux but lengthens the heat pulse, which raises bondline temperature. Peak g depends mainly on gamma, roughly on sqrt(sin gamma). That relation is prior knowledge, but it fits the tabulated g values. D, bluntness and cone are already at their joint limits, and a small D increase to 3.3852 gives a slightly lower flux and temperature at every gamma. The remaining gain is to fill gaps in the gamma curve at D=3.3852, using linear interpolation of the neighbouring evaluated points. I expect each new point to add very little hypervolume. The hypervolume is dominated by the temperature axis, so only a genuinely new low-temperature region could add a lot, and the data show no route into one.\",\"uncertainty\":\"I do not see the full 34-point front or the other 92 feasible designs, so some of these gamma values may sit close to points I was not shown. The gain per point is about 1e-6 to 1e-5 in normalised hypervolume. The last gamma value, -3.570, is within about 4e-5 of the max_g limit and could come out infeasible. Interpolated flux and temperature are accurate to roughly ±1k W/m2 and ±0.3 K. The effect of the tiny D change from 3.385 to 3.3852 is extrapolated from only a few points.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow-gamma end of the curve between -1.55 and -1.65 at maximum D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229170,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cheap interpolation that adds a front point; feasibility is very likely.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.65 and -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231190,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front near the shallow end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.85 and -1.97.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.97 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"The known gap in this region is 0.23° wide.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Second point in the -1.97 to -2.2 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.13},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Reduces the staircase loss in the gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.2 and -2.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.28},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.35 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.42},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247130,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"The -2.5 to -2.78 gap is 0.28° wide, the largest visible; fill it in thirds.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251350,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Largest visible gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Middle point of the -2.5 to -2.78 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":252530,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the largest gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fdf9581b717\",\"rationale\":\"Upper-third point of the same gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"fl